Fix "Unresolved dependencies" gn gen failure on tarball (non-git) checkouts.

In 151.0.7922.71 the two halves of this conditional disagree:

  * action("histograms_xml") is defined only `if (path_exists("//.git"))`
  * but metrics_metadata adds it to deps `if (generate_location_tags)`

We fetch Chromium as a release tarball, so there is no //.git and the
action is never defined - while generate_location_tags is still true, so
the dependency edge is added anyway. gn gen then dies with:

  ERROR Unresolved dependencies.
  //tools/metrics:metrics_metadata(//build/toolchain/linux:clang_arm64)
    needs //tools/metrics:histograms_xml(//build/toolchain/linux:clang_arm64)

Upstream has already corrected this in trunk by switching the group to
the same path_exists("//.git") guard; this is that change backported.
Drop once the pinned Chromium version contains it.

--- a/tools/metrics/BUILD.gn
+++ b/tools/metrics/BUILD.gn
@@ -41,11 +41,11 @@
   ]

   # Only include histograms_xml if we have access to dirmd data, which
-  # is used to populate ownership information. This is only set to false
-  # for non-git checkouts.
+  # is used to populate ownership information. This is disabled
+  # for non-git checkouts, as dirmd doesn't work on non-git checkout.
   # TODO(crbug.com/329080012): Remove this once dirmd works in non-git
   # checkouts.
-  if (generate_location_tags) {
+  if (path_exists("//.git")) {
     deps += [ ":histograms_xml" ]
   }
 }
